IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rda-dates`
IMPORT `rda-claims`

-- Racial Discrimination Act 1975 (Cth), with AHRC Act 1986 ss 3(1), 46P, 46PB, 46PH(1)(b), 46PO, 46POA, 46POB, 46PSA,
-- Federal Court of Australia Act 1976 Part IVA and Acts Interpretation Act 1901 ss 2G, 36 --
-- worked cases for the questions of the person discriminated against.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `s 9 -- racial discrimination in public life`

-- Direct: a public body treats members of a community differently because of race, impairing equal enjoyment of a right.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- what was done to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `unlawful under this section`
-- A distinction because of race that a court finds impairs no human right: s 9 does not reach it.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- what was done to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this section does not reach it on these facts`
-- A distinction not based on race.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- what was done to me` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this section does not reach it on these facts`
-- Indirect (s 9(1A)): an unreasonable requirement I cannot meet, impairing the rights of people of my race.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- what was done to me` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `unlawful under this section`
-- The requirement is reasonable.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- what was done to me` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this section does not reach it on these facts`
-- I can and do comply.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- what was done to me` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this section does not reach it on these facts`
-- It impairs no one's rights.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- what was done to me` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this section does not reach it on these facts`
-- s 9(3): crew engaged overseas for a foreign ship.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- what was done to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not unlawful: the section's own exception applies`
-- s 8(1) special measure; s 8(2) charity; both (special measure answered first).
#ASSERT `s 9 -- what was done to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not unlawful: a special measure (s 8(1))`
#ASSERT `s 9 -- what was done to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not unlawful: it gives effect to a registered charity's provision for people of a particular race (s 8(2))`
#ASSERT `s 9 -- what was done to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not unlawful: a special measure (s 8(1))`
-- Nothing alleged.
#ASSERT `s 9 -- what was done to me` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this section does not reach it on these facts`

§ `s 10 -- equality before the law`

#ASSERT `s 10 -- what s 10 gives me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I enjoy the right to the same extent as people of the other race, by force of s 10(1)`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- what s 10 gives me` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 10 does not apply on these facts`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- what s 10 gives me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not by s 10: the law is a special measure (s 8(1))`
-- s 10(3): a law letting someone else manage an Aboriginal person's property without consent.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- what s 10 gives me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I enjoy the right to manage my own property to the same extent as others, by force of s 10(1) and (3)`
-- The same, though the law is a special measure: s 8(1) excepts s 10(3) measures.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- what s 10 gives me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `I enjoy the right to manage my own property to the same extent as others, by force of s 10(1) and (3)`
-- A Torres Strait Islander.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- what s 10 gives me` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I enjoy the right to manage my own property to the same extent as others, by force of s 10(1) and (3)`
-- The property provision applies to everyone regardless of race.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- what s 10 gives me` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 10 does not apply on these facts`
-- Not an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- what s 10 gives me` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 10 does not apply on these facts`
-- A general property law, but another right is withheld by race: s 10(1) still applies.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- what s 10 gives me` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I enjoy the right to the same extent as people of the other race, by force of s 10(1)`
-- s 3(1): descent from both counts (a Torres Strait Islander; "Aboriginal" excludes them, s 10(3) names both).
#ASSERT `s 3(1) -- I am an Aboriginal or a Torres Strait Islander` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 3(1) -- I am an Aboriginal or a Torres Strait Islander` FALSE FALSE))

