§ `AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- 24 months`

#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- the last day before the complaint is late` (`the calendar date` 15 3 2024) EQUALS `the calendar date` 15 3 2026
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- the last day before the complaint is late` (`the calendar date` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `the calendar date` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- the last day before the complaint is late` (`the calendar date` 31 12 2024) EQUALS `the calendar date` 31 12 2026
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- the last day before the complaint is late` (`the calendar date` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `the calendar date` 31 8 2027
-- AIA s 36(1) item 6 and s 2G(2): an act on 28 February 2022 starts the 24 months on 1 March 2022; they end immediately
-- before 1 March 2024, so the last day is 29 February 2024. The same act a year later: last day 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- the last day before the complaint is late` (`the calendar date` 28 2 2022) EQUALS `the calendar date` 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- the last day before the complaint is late` (`the calendar date` 28 2 2023) EQUALS `the calendar date` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- the last day before the complaint is late` (`the calendar date` 30 6 2025) EQUALS `the calendar date` 30 6 2027
-- Lodged on the last day: not "more than 24 months". The day after: the ground is open.
#ASSERT (NOT (`AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- the President may end my complaint as late` (`the calendar date` 15 3 2024) (`the calendar date` 15 3 2026)))
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- the President may end my complaint as late` (`the calendar date` 15 3 2024) (`the calendar date` 16 3 2026)
#ASSERT (NOT (`AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- the President may end my complaint as late` (`the calendar date` 29 2 2024) (`the calendar date` 28 2 2026)))
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- the President may end my complaint as late` (`the calendar date` 29 2 2024) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2026)
#ASSERT (NOT (`AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- the President may end my complaint as late` (`the calendar date` 28 2 2022) (`the calendar date` 29 2 2024)))
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- the President may end my complaint as late` (`the calendar date` 28 2 2022) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2024)
#ASSERT (NOT (`AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b) -- the President may end my complaint as late` (`the calendar date` 15 3 2024) (`the calendar date` 1 6 2024)))

§ `AHRC Act s 46PO -- going to court`

-- Day 60 is Monday 30 November 2026.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO(2) -- the last day to apply to the court` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) EMPTY EQUALS `the calendar date` 30 11 2026
-- Day 60 is Sunday 13 February 2028 (1 January 2028 is a Saturday): AIA s 36(2) gives Monday 14 February 2028.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO(2) -- the last day to apply to the court` (`the calendar date` 15 12 2027) EMPTY EQUALS `the calendar date` 14 2 2028
-- Day 60 is Wednesday 1 March 2028 (2028 is a leap year).
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO(2) -- the last day to apply to the court` (`the calendar date` 1 1 2028) EMPTY EQUALS `the calendar date` 1 3 2028
-- Day 60 a holiday where the application is made (hypothetical): Tuesday 1 December 2026.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO(2) -- the last day to apply to the court` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) (LIST (`the calendar date` 30 11 2026)) EQUALS `the calendar date` 1 12 2026
-- Notice Monday 26 October 2026: day 60 is Friday 25 December 2026; with 25 and 28 December holidays, Saturday 26 and
-- Sunday 27 passed over, the last day is Tuesday 29 December 2026.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO(2) -- the last day to apply to the court` (`the calendar date` 26 10 2026) (LIST (`the calendar date` 25 12 2026), (`the calendar date` 28 12 2026)) EQUALS `the calendar date` 29 12 2026
-- A holiday that is not the last day changes nothing.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO(2) -- the last day to apply to the court` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) (LIST (`the calendar date` 25 12 2026)) EQUALS `the calendar date` 30 11 2026

-- Terminated as raising an issue of public importance; applied on day 60.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `an issue of public importance the court should consider (s 46PH(1)(h))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 30 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 30 11 2026) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `yes, without needing leave (s 46PO(3A)(b) or (c)), and in time`
-- Terminated as not unlawful discrimination; day 60; leave needed.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `not unlawful discrimination (s 46PH(1)(a))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 30 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 30 11 2026) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `yes, with the court's leave (s 46PO(3A)(a)), and in time`
-- Day 61.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `not unlawful discrimination (s 46PH(1)(a))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `only if the court allows further time (s 46PO(2)) and grants leave (s 46PO(3A)(a))`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `no reasonable prospect of settlement by conciliation (s 46PH(1B)(b))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `only if the court allows further time (s 46PO(2)); no leave needed`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `no reasonable prospect of settlement by conciliation (s 46PH(1B)(b))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026) TRUE EMPTY EQUALS `yes, without needing leave (s 46PO(3A)(b) or (c)), and in time`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `not terminated, or not terminated by the President` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) (`the calendar date` 5 10 2026) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `not yet: the complaint must first be terminated by the President and notice given (s 46PO(1))`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `lodged more than 24 months after the act (s 46PH(1)(b))` FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) (`the calendar date` 5 10 2026) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `not yet: the complaint must first be terminated by the President and notice given (s 46PO(1))`
-- Not yet applied: today is day 45, then day 61.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `no reasonable prospect the court would find unlawful discrimination (s 46PH(1C))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2000) (`the calendar date` 15 11 2026) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `yes, with the court's leave (s 46PO(3A)(a)), and in time`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `no reasonable prospect the court would find unlawful discrimination (s 46PH(1C))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2000) (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `only if the court allows further time (s 46PO(2)) and grants leave (s 46PO(3A)(a))`
-- Applied on the day the notice issued.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `an issue of public importance the court should consider (s 46PH(1)(h))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `yes, without needing leave (s 46PO(3A)(b) or (c)), and in time`
-- Across 29 February 2028: day 60 is 1 March 2028.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `terminated without inquiry (s 46PF(1)(b))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2028) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 3 2028) (`the calendar date` 1 3 2028) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `yes, with the court's leave (s 46PO(3A)(a)), and in time`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `terminated without inquiry (s 46PF(1)(b))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2028) TRUE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2028) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2028) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `only if the court allows further time (s 46PO(2)) and grants leave (s 46PO(3A)(a))`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `terminated at the complainants' request, the respondent being the President, the Commission or a Commissioner (s 46PE)` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2028) TRUE (`the calendar date` 29 2 2028) (`the calendar date` 29 2 2028) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `yes, with the court's leave (s 46PO(3A)(a)), and in time`
-- Day 60 a Sunday (notice 15 December 2027): applying on Sunday 13 or Monday 14 February 2028 is in time (AIA s 36(2)),
-- Tuesday 15 February is not.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `an issue of public importance the court should consider (s 46PH(1)(h))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 15 12 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 13 2 2028) (`the calendar date` 13 2 2028) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `yes, without needing leave (s 46PO(3A)(b) or (c)), and in time`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `an issue of public importance the court should consider (s 46PH(1)(h))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 15 12 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 14 2 2028) (`the calendar date` 14 2 2028) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `yes, without needing leave (s 46PO(3A)(b) or (c)), and in time`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `an issue of public importance the court should consider (s 46PH(1)(h))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 15 12 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 15 2 2028) (`the calendar date` 15 2 2028) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS `only if the court allows further time (s 46PO(2)); no leave needed`
-- Day 60 a holiday: day 61 (Tuesday 1 December 2026) in time; day 62 not.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `not unlawful discrimination (s 46PH(1)(a))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 12 2026) FALSE (LIST (`the calendar date` 30 11 2026)) EQUALS `yes, with the court's leave (s 46PO(3A)(a)), and in time`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO -- can I go to court` `not unlawful discrimination (s 46PH(1)(a))` TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 2 12 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 12 2026) FALSE (LIST (`the calendar date` 30 11 2026)) EQUALS `only if the court allows further time (s 46PO(2)) and grants leave (s 46PO(3A)(a))`

-- The regulative rule directly: 60 days allowed, day 0, day 60, day 61; 61 days allowed (s 36(2)), day 61 and day 62.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO(2) -- an application on this day is in time` 60 0
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO(2) -- an application on this day is in time` 60 60
#ASSERT (NOT (`AHRC Act s 46PO(2) -- an application on this day is in time` 60 61))
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO(2) -- an application on this day is in time` 61 61
#ASSERT (NOT (`AHRC Act s 46PO(2) -- an application on this day is in time` 61 62))

§ `AHRC Act s 46PO(4) -- orders`

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of orders listed in` m MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN JUST l THEN count l
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

#ASSERT `the number of orders listed in` (`AHRC Act s 46PO(4) -- what the court may order` TRUE) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PO(4) -- what the court may order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `AHRC Act ss 46POA, 46POB; FCA Act Part IVA -- group applications`

-- Part IVA (inputs: Part IVA, I make it, I consented, 7 or more, related circumstances, common issue).
-- A community member in a Federal Court class action against a State: no consent needed, may opt out.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act ss 46POA, 46POB -- being included in a group application` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I am a group member without needing to consent (FCA Act s 33E(1)); I may opt out by written notice before the date the court fixes (s 33J(2)), otherwise the judgment binds me (s 33ZB)`
-- Consent given changes nothing under Part IVA.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act ss 46POA, 46POB -- being included in a group application` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I am a group member without needing to consent (FCA Act s 33E(1)); I may opt out by written notice before the date the court fixes (s 33J(2)), otherwise the judgment binds me (s 33ZB)`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act ss 46POA, 46POB -- being included in a group application` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I may commence it as representative party for the group (FCA Act s 33C(1))`
-- Each s 33C(1) element missing in turn.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act ss 46POA, 46POB -- being included in a group application` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: a Part IVA proceeding needs 7 or more claims against the same person, arising out of the same, similar or related circumstances and giving rise to a substantial common issue (FCA Act s 33C(1))`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act ss 46POA, 46POB -- being included in a group application` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: a Part IVA proceeding needs 7 or more claims against the same person, arising out of the same, similar or related circumstances and giving rise to a substantial common issue (FCA Act s 33C(1))`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act ss 46POA, 46POB -- being included in a group application` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: a Part IVA proceeding needs 7 or more claims against the same person, arising out of the same, similar or related circumstances and giving rise to a substantial common issue (FCA Act s 33C(1))`
-- Representative application under s 46PO: the Part IVA inputs do not matter.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act ss 46POA, 46POB -- being included in a group application` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I am the person making it`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act ss 46POA, 46POB -- being included in a group application` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I have consented in writing (s 46POA(1)); I may opt out by written notice before the date the court fixes (s 46POB(3))`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act ss 46POA, 46POB -- being included in a group application` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: it needs my written consent (s 46POA(1))`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act ss 46POA, 46POB -- being included in a group application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: it needs my written consent (s 46POA(1))`

§ `AHRC Act s 46PSA -- costs`

#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PSA(2), (4) -- the respondent pays my costs` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court must order the respondent to pay my costs (s 46PSA(2))`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PSA(2), (4) -- the respondent pays my costs` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes, except the costs my own unreasonable act or omission caused, which the court need not order (s 46PSA(2), (4))`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PSA(2), (4) -- the respondent pays my costs` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I was not successful against this respondent (s 46PSA(2))`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PSA(2), (4) -- the respondent pays my costs` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: I was not successful against this respondent (s 46PSA(2))`

#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PSA(5)-(7) -- I may be ordered to pay costs` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I must not be ordered to pay another party's costs (s 46PSA(5))`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PSA(5)-(7) -- I may be ordered to pay costs` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am not the person who made the representative application (s 46PSA(7))`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PSA(5)-(7) -- I may be ordered to pay costs` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the court may order me to pay: it is satisfied I brought the proceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause (s 46PSA(6)(a))`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PSA(5)-(7) -- I may be ordered to pay costs` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the court may order me to pay the costs my unreasonable act or omission caused the other party (s 46PSA(6)(b))`
-- A respondent of similar standing (an individual against an individual) wins.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PSA(5)-(7) -- I may be ordered to pay costs` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the court may order me to pay: the respondent won and has neither a significant power advantage nor significantly greater resources (s 46PSA(6)(c))`
-- A State or a large employer wins: still protected.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PSA(5)-(7) -- I may be ordered to pay costs` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: I must not be ordered to pay another party's costs (s 46PSA(5))`
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PSA(5)-(7) -- I may be ordered to pay costs` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: I must not be ordered to pay another party's costs (s 46PSA(5))`
-- The respondent did not win and nothing else applies.
#ASSERT `AHRC Act s 46PSA(5)-(7) -- I may be ordered to pay costs` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: I must not be ordered to pay another party's costs (s 46PSA(5))`
